WEBVTT

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.400
The AV-98,
aka the Ingram patrol labor.

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:08.520
6.02 tons.
8.02 meters high.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:12.700
SCB powered.
SCLM drive system.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.990
Armed and ready for combat with a
37 millimeter revolver and stun baton.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:19.540
Designed specifically
for police use...

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:22.200
to make a psychological impact
on the community...

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:25.540
to deter criminals
while making the public feel safe.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.280
yume wo sutenaide
You must not let go of your dreams

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:54.070
me wo sorasanaide
And never turn your gaze away

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:59.080
futari no ai mo kumoru yo
Yet even still love may cloud up and fade away

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:03.450
utsumuita kata wo
And even though you comforted your love

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:06.290
dakishimeta keredo
When he was feeling down

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:11.300
samishisa mune ni tsumotta
Sadness was still weighing down his heavy heart

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:18.510
yume wa kimi no buki no hazu da yo
Hang on tight to your dreams - they're weapons in your arsenal

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:25.270
nee da kara kanashimi mo kinukete itte
You'll find that you can get through anything at all

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:31.440
so never cry itsu mo kimi wo mitsumete 'ru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be watching over you

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:37.280
fair na ikikata no kimi ga suki
What I love about you is your strong sense of fairness

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:43.790
so never cry itsu mo kimi no soba ni iru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be right there by your side

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:49.460
da kara mata asu e kakedashite
And so now you can face your future fearlessly

00:01:57.130 --> 00:02:01.140
The Suspicious Pair

00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:15.780
Been waiting long?

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:18.400
I think you've been stood up.

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:19.740
Your boyfriend's a no-show.

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:22.870
But you could catch a movie with me!

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:23.870
Get lost.

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:26.620
Let's watch videos, over at my place!

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:27.330
Beat it.

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:28.580
Harsh.

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:32.460
I have every anime
show from the 80's!

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:37.300
- Geez, sorry!
- She's a policewoman?

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:41.260
Do you have a minute?

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:44.050
Have you been saved by God?

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:50.730
Been waiting long?

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:03.490
Are you still pouting?

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:06.040
Sorry I was 10 minutes late.

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:10.830
But arriving 10 minutes
early was YOUR fault.

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:15.380
In that 20 minutes, two creeps
and a street preacher hit on me!

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:17.420
It was terrible.

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:18.460
Creeps?

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:20.760
There're a lot of
weirdos in this world.

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:21.970
Whatever you say...

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:25.390
I know! After the movie,
I'll buy you a cup of coffee.

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:26.640
No.

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:27.640
What?

00:03:28.390 --> 00:03:29.850
You'll buy me a chocolate parfait!

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:32.020
Okay.

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:37.780
- You know...
- Yeah?

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:40.990
What are we doing here?

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:42.150
Having a snack...

00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:46.490
I mean... it's our day off.

00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:51.500
Why are we sitting here
reading movie programs?

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:54.500
Because it isn't time for dinner yet?

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:58.750
Food and movies.
Isn't there anything else to do?

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:00.460
So what do you want to do?

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:04.300
Something BIG,
so we don't waste our vacation!

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:05.800
Something big...

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:17.150
Is this better than
sitting in the coffee shop?

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:22.240
Look at that!

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:24.610
Patlabor?

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:32.330
Damn! I can't get past mission 3!

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:34.250
Yeah, me neither.

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:36.960
My turn!

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:51.470
You know what you're doing?

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:54.480
You're supposed to read
the instructions first!

00:04:55.230 --> 00:05:00.270
So this is how you move,
this is the trigger...

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:04.570
This is nothing like the real thing!
And these foot pedals!

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:07.030
Pay attention! The game's starting!

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:10.490
Shield! Button B!

00:05:10.490 --> 00:05:11.910
Where? Which one!

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:21.550
The scene changed.

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:25.630
The impact spun you. Turn around.

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:27.890
The criminal's gone!

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:30.720
Switch to the map.
That'll show you where he is.

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:33.060
There he is!

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:35.020
Get with the program!

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:37.480
This is hard!

00:05:37.810 --> 00:05:41.520
Silence! The pilot must always
obey the command car.

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:42.570
Listen!

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:45.360
Nice try.

00:05:47.110 --> 00:05:48.950
The controls need adjusting.

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:50.240
Skill would help...

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:51.030
How dare you!

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:52.870
Watch a pro.

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:03.460
I was watching...

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:05.670
You're right. It <i>is</i> hard!

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:09.970
This simply won't do.

00:06:09.970 --> 00:06:15.720
I think it's time I stepped in here.

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:16.930
What do you think?

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:18.270
Who are...

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:19.270
You?

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:22.560
You may call me "The Black Knight."

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:38.290
Another one!

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:40.960
One more and he'll finish the game!

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:46.170
And so it ends.

00:06:47.880 --> 00:06:49.130
Missed him!

00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:50.680
He's getting away!

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:52.850
Please! I have to see the ending!

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:54.260
Very well.

00:06:58.600 --> 00:06:59.560
Watch this.

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:06.690
This guy's incredible!

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:15.160
Thanks to your superb piloting, the city is once again at peace.

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:22.710
<i>Rating: Police Commissioner.</i>

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:41.940
Thank you, thank you.
Thank you for your support.

00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:47.730
You've just witnessed perfect technique.
Care to challenge me?

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:48.730
Uhh...

00:07:49.190 --> 00:07:54.490
I'm as good as you can get
without having a real Labor.

00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:55.990
Asuma!

00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:01.370
Do you have more quarters?

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:02.210
Not again!

00:08:02.790 --> 00:08:07.630
My reputation is on the line!
No game's gonna make a fool out of me!

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:12.300
This time, I'll finish level 2!

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:15.840
That won't be much of a reputation.

00:08:18.970 --> 00:08:21.600
So how did the action and movement feel?

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:24.140
The game was fine, but...

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:25.400
Yes?

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:31.280
It's the idea that there are
hordes of armed, killer Labors...

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:33.610
Too hard to swallow?

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:37.370
Most Labors today are
construction machines.

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:40.330
Ah, but what about the future?

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:42.120
Excuse me.

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:45.790
Bud! Bud Renard!
What are you doing here?

00:08:46.250 --> 00:08:52.010
Mr. Utsumi, you aced level 10!
I can't get past level 9 yet.

00:08:52.010 --> 00:08:55.260
It just takes a great deal of practice.

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:59.430
I'm no competition for you.
I have blisters, from all my practice.

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:03.770
Besides, I have a far
better toy for you.

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:08.360
I'll be happy after I finish level 10 -
just once.

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:10.400
All right. Just once.

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:11.900
Once is all I need.

00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:17.610
This game is a lot harder
than the real thing!

00:09:17.610 --> 00:09:18.450
Hey, miss!

00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:19.910
Trade places?

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:23.200
It's pretty hard.

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:25.500
I know. Hold out your hand!

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:26.120
Like this?

00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:29.380
I'll avenge you! Watch me!

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:34.670
I guess he wasn't as
good as you can get.

00:09:36.630 --> 00:09:40.300
So Izumi was avenged by some little kid?

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:43.270
You know, some kids have a gift.

00:09:43.270 --> 00:09:45.730
That's pathetic!

00:09:45.730 --> 00:09:48.310
You've never even played it,
so you don't know.

00:09:48.850 --> 00:09:51.770
Let me at it! Bring it in here!

00:09:51.770 --> 00:09:53.650
Right... bring it in the bath, huh?

00:09:53.980 --> 00:09:56.990
Then don't tell me what
I can or can't do!

00:09:56.990 --> 00:09:58.200
What's your problem, man?

00:09:58.450 --> 00:09:59.110
I'm getting out!

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:04.870
Why you!

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:19.760
So you were in the arcade all this time.

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:22.220
The company was looking for you.

00:10:22.220 --> 00:10:25.020
Half those machines are made by us...

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:28.810
and market research is
part of my job, isn't it?

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:32.690
The managers don't seem
to feel that way.

00:10:32.690 --> 00:10:37.570
Who cares what they think.
We're doing exactly what we need to do.

00:10:37.570 --> 00:10:41.660
Mr. Utsumi, is that my new toy?

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:43.990
No, that one's gone.

00:10:43.990 --> 00:10:46.160
It was destroyed?

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:49.410
Why don't you answer that, Kurosaki?

00:10:49.410 --> 00:10:51.120
You're a tough boss.

00:10:51.580 --> 00:10:52.920
I've had plenty of time
to think about it.

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:56.590
Labor combat comes
down to hand-to-hand.

00:10:56.920 --> 00:11:02.550
Exactly. Why load a Labor down with
fancy beams and weapons?

00:11:02.930 --> 00:11:07.270
What we really want is
the hand-to-hand data.

00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:10.730
So the Phantom was
child's play for Griffin?

00:11:11.230 --> 00:11:14.150
Just wait until we show the world...

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:17.150
Mr. Utsumi, look! It's that lady!

00:11:21.530 --> 00:11:22.820
You know her?

00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:24.700
We met today.

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:31.540
Show a little restraint, Chief!
If you don't...

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:33.460
I'm feeling good about this one.

00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:08.370
Got you!

00:12:09.910 --> 00:12:12.250
That isn't like her.

00:12:12.250 --> 00:12:18.210
That's high praise for you.
Izumi will be happy to hear it!

00:12:18.210 --> 00:12:21.130
Don't be an idiot!
Go check the data backups.

00:12:27.930 --> 00:12:29.260
Drat!

00:12:30.100 --> 00:12:35.230
Flexibility wins over power.
Alphonse is still number one!

00:12:35.230 --> 00:12:36.520
Don't get carried away.

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:41.490
It was just practice.
A real foe wouldn't go so easy on you.

00:12:41.490 --> 00:12:42.240
But -

00:12:42.440 --> 00:12:44.700
In a real fight there are no "buts!"

00:12:44.700 --> 00:12:46.910
You're talking about weapons, right?

00:12:47.870 --> 00:12:51.580
Wrestling is okay, but target
practice is the important work!

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:52.700
Ota...

00:12:52.700 --> 00:12:56.500
I was watching. You're getting better.

00:12:56.500 --> 00:12:58.920
Thanks to you, Lieutenant!

00:12:58.920 --> 00:13:03.220
Thank you for saying that,
but there's room for improvement.

00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:04.670
We'll take some extra practice,
beginning today.

00:13:12.220 --> 00:13:15.390
I saw your report, but we need
accuracy right now.

00:13:15.390 --> 00:13:19.060
We've pushed speed and
accuracy to the limit.

00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:23.070
I'll need to check the parts and
materials list, one last time.

00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:26.030
This is going to cost quite a bit.

00:13:26.570 --> 00:13:29.200
We're well under cost for
ten combat models.

00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:32.290
But diverting the production line...

00:13:32.740 --> 00:13:34.660
You aren't a businessman.

00:13:35.210 --> 00:13:39.250
I've told you time and again
to spare no expense on this Labor.

00:13:40.170 --> 00:13:42.550
It'll put our division in the red.

00:13:42.550 --> 00:13:46.720
Don't worry.
The other divisions can cover us.

00:13:47.380 --> 00:13:49.550
From space shuttles to toothpicks,

00:13:50.680 --> 00:13:52.720
Shaft can do anything.

00:13:53.220 --> 00:13:54.020
Hey, Bud!

00:14:05.740 --> 00:14:08.530
This is your new toy.

00:14:48.360 --> 00:14:50.070
You look happy.

00:14:51.660 --> 00:14:53.450
When can I try it out?

00:14:53.870 --> 00:14:56.290
One more week of construction...

00:14:56.290 --> 00:14:59.120
and two weeks of adjustments after that.

00:14:59.120 --> 00:15:00.370
That's so long!

00:15:00.710 --> 00:15:04.340
They're putting in plenty of overtime
on this. Be patient.

00:15:05.300 --> 00:15:09.380
And just for fun, we have
a special treat for tonight.

00:15:09.380 --> 00:15:09.930
What?

00:15:10.590 --> 00:15:14.010
You said you wanted to
see an Ingram in action.

00:15:20.520 --> 00:15:23.060
Polishing again?

00:15:23.770 --> 00:15:27.150
I'd rather help with his maintenance.

00:15:27.150 --> 00:15:30.740
But since I can't do that,
at least I can polish him.

00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:33.530
Maybe I can find a few things
you could help with.

00:15:33.530 --> 00:15:36.370
Really? You'll teach me?

00:15:36.990 --> 00:15:39.450
But the boss might not like it.

00:15:39.450 --> 00:15:40.000
Why not?

00:15:40.580 --> 00:15:42.920
He's a traditional artisan to the core.

00:15:42.920 --> 00:15:45.960
He wouldn't like a woman
fiddling with his machines.

00:15:45.960 --> 00:15:47.000
Shige.

00:15:47.420 --> 00:15:51.720
I'm going home. Take care
of Division 1 when they get back.

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:54.140
Machine 2 is still practicing.

00:15:54.140 --> 00:15:56.010
Yes, Sir! Good night!

00:15:56.010 --> 00:15:56.970
And one more thing.

00:15:58.680 --> 00:16:02.980
There are male cooks
and secretaries, you know.

00:16:03.230 --> 00:16:06.020
If she doesn't interfere with our work,
go ahead and teach her.

00:16:06.440 --> 00:16:07.730
Yes Sir!

00:16:08.110 --> 00:16:10.110
Thank you, Mr. Sakaki!

00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:16.450
Rinko Ward, section 21,
construction site:

00:16:16.450 --> 00:16:18.660
A Labor is making terrorist demands.

00:16:18.660 --> 00:16:22.870
The Labor appears to be a Saturn type.
Division 2, mobilize.

00:16:22.870 --> 00:16:26.330
I missed my chance to go home.
Well, hurry up!

00:16:26.330 --> 00:16:29.800
Swap batteries on machine 2!
Load the carriers!

00:16:42.850 --> 00:16:46.860
I just finished that
foundation yesterday!

00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:51.860
I had to cancel a date
to make that schedule!

00:16:51.860 --> 00:16:53.610
How dare you ruin my hard work!

00:17:12.340 --> 00:17:15.340
The Saturn's not too bad,
but I can't say I like it.

00:17:15.880 --> 00:17:17.640
You're sure the Ingram will come?

00:17:17.890 --> 00:17:20.970
Division 1 is already dealing with
a distraction I created.

00:17:21.390 --> 00:17:26.310
They have to send the Ingrams.

00:17:36.780 --> 00:17:39.950
Here it is. Okay Bud, watch closely.

00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:43.410
How should we handle it?

00:17:43.410 --> 00:17:47.080
He's violent, so the first thing is to
make him lose his temper.

00:17:47.750 --> 00:17:49.130
Let's go.

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:52.340
Submit!

00:18:38.840 --> 00:18:39.970
Good.

00:18:39.970 --> 00:18:40.840
It's not good.

00:18:42.010 --> 00:18:45.060
Noa, what are you doing?
Go help machine 2!

00:18:50.810 --> 00:18:54.860
This is much better than
watching her on video.

00:18:57.280 --> 00:18:58.780
Come at me!

00:19:07.200 --> 00:19:08.080
Bad move!

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:11.290
What's she doing?
She should have been able to avoid that.

00:19:11.790 --> 00:19:13.710
Whose side are you on?

00:19:15.920 --> 00:19:19.380
Izumi, if you let him get away,
I'll pummel you!

00:19:24.100 --> 00:19:25.050
I got him!

00:19:40.200 --> 00:19:41.860
Take that!

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:45.620
Ota, you're too violent.

00:19:46.330 --> 00:19:51.290
He's the violent one!
Look at that face!

00:19:51.710 --> 00:19:56.750
She had to let the cable out all the
way to use it as a weapon.

00:19:57.130 --> 00:20:00.970
I didn't think she'd have the nerve.

00:20:01.720 --> 00:20:08.100
She trusts her machine.
That takes real courage.

00:20:08.600 --> 00:20:10.640
She'll be a tough opponent.

00:20:10.850 --> 00:20:15.230
Very true.
This is going to be a lot of fun.

00:20:15.310 --> 00:20:16.110
Yeah.

00:20:24.740 --> 00:20:27.240
Asuma, the pilot's getting away!

00:20:29.410 --> 00:20:32.580
Captain, call the riot squad!

00:20:33.040 --> 00:20:38.840
I can't. We haven't secured
the area yet. Besides...

00:20:38.840 --> 00:20:39.750
Besides?

00:20:39.750 --> 00:20:42.670
The riot squad never arrived.

00:20:44.630 --> 00:20:47.350
What are you looking at ME for?

00:20:58.900 --> 00:21:03.240
I saw the video of the latest fight.
The Ingram is quite a machine.

00:21:03.240 --> 00:21:04.610
Will your new machine be a match?

00:21:05.410 --> 00:21:09.080
Definitely. Its capabilities
will exceed the Ingram's.

00:21:09.080 --> 00:21:11.740
But we had to push the
systems way past their specs.

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:16.920
I don't care. I told you,
we aren't offering this commercially.

00:21:17.790 --> 00:21:19.670
I'm glad to hear that.

00:21:20.090 --> 00:21:23.800
I've done everything I could,
since you gave the go-ahead.

00:21:35.060 --> 00:21:36.100
Here it is:

00:21:36.100 --> 00:21:42.070
Shaft Japan, Tsuchiura Research
Laboratories production, type J9.

00:21:43.480 --> 00:21:44.530
The Griffin.

00:21:47.820 --> 00:21:52.580
It's the culmination of
everything we've learned.

00:21:52.870 --> 00:21:56.000
It should make Bud's job a simple one.

00:21:57.920 --> 00:22:02.340
Two more weeks.
I can't wait to see it in action.

00:22:42.630 --> 00:22:45.840
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:22:45.960 --> 00:22:49.550
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:22:51.890 --> 00:22:55.810
